# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-list-hosts-ignored — alfe --list-hosts is accepted and does nothing
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-list-hosts-ignored

* Symptom

Split out of =alfe-host-selection-gaps= (alfe 2.2.77). The shared parser
accepts =--list-hosts= and sets =list-hosts-p=, but =alfe.cli:run= has no
branch for it, so with no other action alfe opens its REPL (=alfe> =) instead
of printing the hosts as =clautolisp --list-hosts= does. =--help= does not
list the option, and the user manual says alfe accepts it and does nothing.

* Proposal

Print the hosts and exit 0, like =--list-encodings= / =--list-dialects=. The
shared =clautolisp.autolisp-cli:print-hosts= prints a line about the retired
spellings of two hosts; alfe, which dropped them, should not repeat it, so
either alfe prints its own three lines or the shared list loses that note
(clautolisp-visible). Then: =--help=, the man page, the manual's "Host
selection" (the "Two clautolisp options alfe does not have" paragraph), a
scenario.

* Acceptance criteria

- =alfe --list-hosts= prints cador, cadtui, nihil with a one-line summary
  each and exits 0, opening no REPL.
- Documented in =--help=, the man page and the user manual.

* Resolved — alfe 2.2.107

=alfe.cli:run= gained the branch, beside =--list-encodings= and
=--list-dialects=, and prints through the shared
=clautolisp.autolisp-cli:print-hosts=.

The proposal's open question is answered the first way it offered: the
SHARED list keeps its aliases note for clautolisp, and =print-hosts= takes
=:aliases= (default T) which alfe passes NIL. alfe refuses =mock=, =null=
and =none= -- =cli-host-cador-cadtui-and-nihil= pins that -- so printing
the note would have advertised spellings it rejects, and changing the
shared list for everyone would have taken the note away from clautolisp,
where it is true.

#+begin_example
$ alfe --list-hosts
Available --host backends:
  cador    Headless CAD core: the /application/console tree (default).
  cadtui   Full textual UI-tree host on the cador core: menus, drawings,
            CAD view, and DCL dialogs mirrored into an inspectable tree.
  nihil    Trivial backend: no CAD host at all.
#+end_example

Documented in all three places the rule asks for: the =--help= banner
(beside =--list-dialects=), the man page OPTIONS section, and the user
manual -- whose /Two clautolisp options alfe does not have/ section said
alfe "accepts =--list-hosts= without doing anything with it" and is now
=** --list-hosts= with the output above, plus /One clautolisp option alfe
does not have/ for =--mock-input=, which is still true.

Tests: =cli-run-list-hosts-prints-the-backends-and-exits-zero= (prints the
three, exits 0, no =aliases:=, no =mock=, no =alfe>=),
=cli-list-hosts-sets-its-slot=, and the corpus scenario
=tests/scenarios/cli/list-hosts.sexp= -- verified to really run and pass
(=:STATUS :PASS=, exit 0) rather than to be silently skipped. alfe suite
1210 checks, 0 failures.
